type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-16"
# Concept DOI: it resolves to the latest archived release, so it never needs
# bumping alongside `version`. The v0.1.0-specific DOI is in preferred-citation.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23053349"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZengZichao/ChartExtractor"
keywords:
  - chart digitization
  - data extraction
  - figure analysis
  - offline
  - desktop
  - tauri
  - rust
abstract: >-
  ChartExtractor is a fully offline desktop application for extracting numerical
  data from charts in scientific papers (bitmap images and PDF). It calibrates
  axes from four user-picked reference points with linear or logarithmic affine
  transforms, traces curves by colour-mask column scanning, detects scatter
  points by blob clustering, supports manual point editing, grid detection,
  batch folder processing and project save/restore, and exports xlsx / CSV /
  JSON with optional metadata comment lines compatible with pandas.read_csv.
  All processing runs locally: no network calls are made, and no data leaves the
  machine. The interface is bilingual (Chinese / English) with light and dark
  themes.
